{start_of_verse: Intro Verse}
[G]Oh a long long time [G]ago when I [C]left my home to [G]roam
[G]Down in the [G]hills of [D7]Tennessee[D7]
[G]There's the sweetest [G]little girl [C]that was ever in this [G]world
[G]Down in the [D7]hills of [G]Tennessee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh that [C]little girl of [C]mine in [G]Tennessee[G]
[G]I know she's [G]waiting there for [D7]me[D7]
[G]Someday I'll settle [G]down in that [C]little country [G]town
[G]With that little girl of [D7]mine in [G]Tennessee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
She begged me not to go, you'll be sorry dear, I know
For the way that you've been treating me
I have rambled all around but there's no one else I've found
Who could take the place of her in Tennessee
{end_of_verse}

